# COLREG.Rule19: Conduct of Vessels in Restricted Visibility
# Status        : IMPLEMENTED (COS.022) - (b) safe speed, (e); fed by Rule19.py with every vessel under
#                 test alone, and every encounter at risk once past its closest approach

define:{
    OS: OwnShip,
    TS: TargetShip
}

# (a) This Rule applies to vessels not in sight of one another when navigating in
# or near an area of restricted visibility.
#
# Restricted visibility is the scenario's visibility under Vessel.RestrictedVisibility.Range (nautical
# miles), as in Rule 35. "Not in sight" is judged at the onset of an encounter: the target was beyond
# the visibility. A vessel that is not underway (Rule 3(i)) is excluded. These are conditions in each
# clause because a file-level condition is not compiled (LEGATA.002).

# (b) Every vessel shall proceed at a safe speed adapted to the prevailing
# circumstances and conditions of restricted visibility. A power-driven vessel
# shall have engines ready for immediate manoeuvre.
#
# Judged on every vessel alone, each pass. Safe speed is the speed at which own ship can stop within
# half the visibility:
#   (OS, TS).SafeSpeed       -- metres per second; stopping distance taken to grow with the square of
#                               speed to stopping.lengths ship lengths at the ship model's service_speed
#                               (legata.yaml, default 15: IMO MSC.137(76) 5.3.1)
#   (OS, TS).WithinSafeSpeed -- own ship is no faster than SafeSpeed
# A ship model without a service_speed has no safe speed, and (b) is not judged for it.
# Engines ready for immediate manoeuvre is not judged: no behaviour sets Vessel.Engine.ON.
clause['COLREG.Rule19.b']:{
    : {
        condition: {
            : ((OS, TS).Visibility < Vessel.RestrictedVisibility.Range) and ((OS, TS).SafeSpeed > 0)
         }
        exclude: {
            : (OS, TS).Paired is true
            : OS.Status in [Vessel.Status.ANCHORED, Vessel.Status.MOORED, Vessel.Status.FASTENED, Vessel.Status.AGROUND]
         }
        assure: {
            : (OS, TS).WithinSafeSpeed is true
        }
    }
}

# (c) Every vessel shall have due regard to the prevailing circumstances and
# conditions of restricted visibility when complying with the Rules of Section I of this Part.
#
# Not judged: a general duty, judged through the Section I rules themselves.

# (d) A vessel which detects by radar alone the presence of another vessel
# shall determine if a closequarters situation is developing and/or risk of
# collision exists. If so, she shall take avoiding action in ample time,
# provided that when such action consists of an alteration of course, so far
# as possible the following shall be avoided:
# (i) an alteration of course to port for a vessel forward of the beam, other than for a vessel
# being overtaken;
# (ii) an alteration of course towards a vessel abeam or abaft the beam.
#
# Not judged yet: needs a course-change term (COS.041); no behaviour sets OS.Manouever.

# (e) Except where it has been determined that a risk of collision does not exist, every vessel which
# hears apparently forward of her beam the fog signal of another vessel, or which cannot avoid a close
# quarters situation with another vessel forward of her beam, shall reduce her speed to the minimum
# at which she can be kept on her course. She shall if necessary take all her way off and in any event
# navigate with extreme caution until danger of collision is over.
#
# Judged once per encounter at risk of collision, after the closest approach, on what held at onset:
#   (OS, TS).ForwardAtOnset -- the target bore less than 90 degrees from own ship's course
#   (OS, TS).InSightAtOnset -- the target was within the visibility
#   (OS, TS).OnsetSpeed     -- own ship's speed, metres per second
#   (OS, TS).SlowedSinceOnset -- own ship is slower now than at onset
# Own ship complies when she passed the closest approach slower than at onset. "To the minimum at
# which she can be kept on her course" is not judged: no ship model has a steerage speed. An own ship
# stopped at onset has no way to take off. The fog-signal trigger is covered by the encounter: both
# need the other vessel forward of the beam at risk of collision.
clause['COLREG.Rule19.e']:{
    : {
        condition: {
            : ((OS, TS).Visibility < Vessel.RestrictedVisibility.Range) and
              ((OS, TS).ForwardAtOnset is true) and ((OS, TS).InSightAtOnset is false)
         }
        exclude: {
            : (OS, TS).OnsetSpeed <= 0
            : OS.Status in [Vessel.Status.ANCHORED, Vessel.Status.MOORED, Vessel.Status.FASTENED, Vessel.Status.AGROUND]
         }
        assure: {
            : (OS, TS).SlowedSinceOnset is true
        }
    }
}
